        "original_id": "0acec6cc-8823-5295-86b9-32df343641e7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Breeds: Large Münsterländer, Bracco Italiano, German Longhaired Pointer\n- Places: Münster region, Germany, Italy\n- Concepts: gun dogs, breed relationships\n\nFacts:\n- The Large Münsterländer, also called the Großer Münsterländer, is a breed of gun dog originally from the Münster region in Germany.\n- The Bracco Italiano is a breed of dog developed in Italy as a versatile gun dog.\n- The German Longhaired Pointer is closely related to the German Shorthaired Pointer, the German Wirehaired Pointer, and the Large Münsterländer.\n- The Large Münsterländer was previously part of the German Longhaired Pointer breed.",
